      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey can u help me understand this part of an nda i just got? it says: \"The Receiving Party shall indemnify, defend, and hold harmless the Disclosing Party from and against any and all losses, damages, liabilities, costs, and expenses (including reasonable attorneys' fees) arising out of or resulting from any breach of this Agreement or any unauthorized use of the Confidential Information by the Receiving Party or its Representatives.\" basically what does this mean for me if i mess up?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This clause means that if you (the Receiving Party) break the NDA or misuse the confidential information—whether directly or through your team or agents—you’re personally on the hook for all resulting costs, including legal fees. In plain terms, if you leak or mishandle the info, you’ll have to pay for the other side’s losses and their lawyers, not just your own. It’s a broad indemnity, so even accidental breaches can trigger it, and it shifts the financial risk almost entirely onto you. Before signing, you might want to negotiate a cap on liability or carve out for gross negligence only. But yes, if you mess up, this is the clause that makes you pay—and pay big.",
