      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. so it sounds pretty risky. it says \"or its Representatives\" too... does that mean i'm responsible if like, a sub-contractor i hire leaks something? that seems like a lot of hidden stuff to keep track of.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, exactly—\"Representatives\" typically includes your employees, agents, consultants, and sub-contractors. So if a sub-contractor you hired to help with a project accidentally shares the confidential info, you’re still the one who has to cover the damages and legal costs. It’s a strict liability setup, meaning you don’t get a pass just because you didn’t personally leak it. You’d need to have airtight NDAs and training with anyone you bring in, and even then, the risk stays on you. It’s a lot of hidden responsibility, but that’s why these clauses are so heavily negotiated. If you can, try to narrow \"Representatives\" to only those you directly control, or add a clause that you’re only liable if you failed to use reasonable care in supervising them. Otherwise, you’re essentially acting as an insurer for everyone you work with.",
      "source": "target",
